         <div type="bio">
            <p>Irish poet and literary critic. After military service in WWI, MacGreevy earned a degree at Trinity College Dublin and worked as an art critic in Dublin. He met JJ in Paris in 1924. While living in Paris, he helped JJ correct proofs for <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">transition</name> magazine, contributed an essay to <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Our Exagmination Round His Factification for Incamination of Work in Progress</name> (Paris: Shakespeare and Company, 1929), and contributed poetry and criticism to numerous literary magazines. Returning to Dublin, he published his <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Poems</name> (London: Heinemann, 1934) and became Director of the National Gallery in 1950. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
